%description:
A base station node (eNodeB, and gNodeB, which extends it) had a txPower parameter, 100mw by
default, that nothing read: the base station transmits with its PHY's eNodeBTxPower (46 dBm by
default; microTxPower in a micro cell). An ini file that set the node's txPower ran without a
message at another power than it asked for. Setting it is an error at initialization, which
names the parameter to set. The value is written in the parameter's declared unit, mw, the
form that ran.

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = simu5g.test.moduletest.lib.NrSessionTestNetwork

*.gnb.txPower = 100mw

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%exitcode: 1
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stderr
The base station node's 'txPower' parameter is read by nothing: the base station transmits with the power of its PHY. Set cellularNic.phy.eNodeBTxPower instead (cellularNic.phy.microTxPower in a micro cell)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
